# Installed by the retrobox-system-settings package (/etc/sudoers.d): sudo
# shows an asterisk for each character typed at its password prompt, so what
# is typed can be seen, in a terminal and in the overlay's task screen (an
# emulator's installer asking for its build dependencies), where a controller
# or an on-screen keyboard types it. Remove this file to go back to sudo's
# silent prompt.
Defaults pwfeedback
